From 20faf4735ce2e2fe5e9ff3b921ec5c30dc0bcc64 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:51:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tui): single-flight profile roster memo fills [daveey]

profiles.list runs on the serve's 8-thread RPC pool, and Desktop asks for it several times at connect.
Each per-profile memo (session fields, reader session fields, ui_meta) only filled on completion, so
every concurrent cold caller recomputed every profile. On the hub (68768e45, 11 profiles, live store)
a concurrent burst of 6 cold calls cost 3.99-4.72 s of process CPU; the same 6 calls in sequence cost
0.25-0.43 s. The live P1 of serve 1231378 shows the burst: 6 runs in the first 68 s, 0.96 s CPU,
max 0.50 s per call, the bulk of the whole-RPC row's profiles.list share (0.27% of core in the
whole-row replay).

Five whys:
1. Why does the startup cost ~4 s? 6 profiles.list calls each recompute 11 profiles' session fields.
2. Why each? They run concurrently on the RPC pool and the memo is empty until the first finishes.
3. Why concurrently? Desktop's connect fires several roster reads; the serve dispatches each to the pool.
4. Why no sharing? `_cached` had no notion of a fill in progress.
5. Why not caught? Tests and benches called the handler sequentially; no test drove concurrent misses.

Fix: `_cached` keeps a per-memo table of running fills. A miss whose signature EQUALS a running fill's
waits for it and returns a copy of what it stored, which is exactly the value a hit right after it would
return. A different signature (input moved), no signature (racy mtime / no store), a same-thread re-entry,
a leader failure or a join longer than 30 s all compute as before. Only the current fill for a key stores,
so a superseded or invalidated fill never overwrites a newer memo; invalidate() drops running fills too.
No TTL, no staleness, no change to what is read, who may read it, or redaction.

Proof:
- tests/tui_gateway/test_profile_roster_cache_singleflight.py (11 tests). RED on the base: the public-API
  test sees 4 computes for one unchanged store (the rest need the new internals). GREEN: all pass, 15
  repeated runs; 48 consumer files, 728 tests pass; scripts/check ok.
- Hub A/B, real patched module in a separate process, 6 concurrent cold calls, 4 runs each:
  base 3990/4324/4720/4580 ms CPU, fix 642/654/1029/604 ms CPU; every call returns all 11 profiles.
